# 1. CRITICAL CUSTOMER FEEDBACK

The customer has reviewed the current School forwarding interface and identified two remaining problems.

### Problem A — Official document entry is unnecessarily complicated

The reviewer has already received or prepared the official signed School decision/proposal document.

The system currently requires manual inputs such as:

- Document number.
- Issue date.
- Signatory name.
- Signatory position.
- Official PDF attachment.

This is unnecessary for the intended user interaction.

**The authorized School Reviewer should only need to upload the official PDF.**

Do not force them to manually transcribe information already contained in the document.

### Problem B — The sidebar and business flows are unnecessarily fragmented

The current School navigation contains potentially overlapping destinations:

- Tổng quan.
- Hồ sơ sinh viên.
- Cần xét sơ tuyển.
- Yêu cầu bổ sung.
- Danh sách đề nghị Thành phố.
- Đã chuyển Thành phố.
- Thống kê.
- Thông báo.

Some may be separate routes for different filters or statuses of the same underlying workflow.

This creates unnecessary navigation, duplicated application lists and confusing business states.

**The customer wants a small number of intuitive destinations organized around real staff tasks.**

Do not simply rename menu items.

Audit and remove actual UX duplication while preserving every legitimate capability.

